/*
 * Self-hosted, base64-embedded (Chromium/Playwright loads this CSS from an
 * in-memory HTML string, not a served directory, so relative font URLs
 * would not resolve reliably).
 *
 * TrueType (glyf-outline) instances, not the .otf (CFF/PostScript-outline)
 * originals: Chromium's PDF backend (Skia) can only embed glyf-outline
 * fonts as a proper /Type0 CID font. A CFF-flavored font gets exported as
 * a Type3 font instead, one throwaway sub-font per handful of glyphs, with
 * roughly one font-resource switch every couple of characters. Apple's
 * PDFKit (Preview.app copy/paste) can't reliably reconstruct word
 * boundaries from that structure and inserts phantom mid-word spaces
 * (e.g. "SIL" -> "S IL", "CI/CD" -> "C I /CD") even though nothing is
 * visibly wrong on the page. These files are static wght instances
 * generated from Vercel'''s variable Geist/Geist Mono fonts with
 * fonttools varLib.instancer, since only the variable .ttf ships glyf
 * outlines (the static release is CFF/.otf only).
 */

@font-face {
  font-family: "Geist";
  font-style: normal;
  font-weight: 400;
  font-display: block;
  src: url(data:font/ttf;base64,) format("truetype");
}

